      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`InterleaveCPStrategy._interleave_shard` explicitly handles Python lists and tuples, but indexes them with a `range`. Both types raise `TypeError`, including for empty sequences. This is a fix for the supported sequence branch; the Tensor path is unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUse strided slicing to preserve the input sequence type. Add regression coverage through `shard_local_tokens` for list/tuple, empty/short/uneven/divisible lengths, CP sizes 1/2/4, and every rank. Check values, type, and input immutability.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nCPU, Python 3.12 / PyTorch 2.13.0:\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=999 PYTHONPATH=python python test/registered/cp/test_cp_strategy_unit.py\n```\n\n- Before the fix: the new test fails with `TypeError` in all 56 subcases.\n- After the fix: the full file passes, 25 tests.\n- `pre-commit run --files python/sglang/srt/layers/cp/interleave.py test/registered/cp/test_cp_strategy_unit.py` passes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: no Tensor/kernel changes or performance claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add focused registered unit coverage.\n- [x] Documentation: not needed for this existing behavior.\n- [x] Accuracy/speed: CPU regression above; no model-output or speed claim.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and testing.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35512900578](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35512900578)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35512900442](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35512900442)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35512900521](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35512900521)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
